+# Desktop Client Isolation Review (Package-07 Attempt)
+
+Date: 2026-09-12  
+Author: Gemini (Security Review Worker)  
+Scope: Source-only analysis of the package-07 Claude Desktop isolation failure  
+
+---
+
+## Executive Summary
+
+The package-07 Claude Desktop acceptance attempt did not achieve isolated containment. Statically extracted startup code from the packaged Electron binary demonstrates that `claude.exe` deletes the `CLAUDE_USER_DATA_DIR` environment variable during early startup unless developer authorization (`CLAUDE_CDP_AUTH`) is present and cryptographically verified. As a result, the application did not use the integrator's prepared configuration directory (`run/user-data`), but reverted to the default user profile path, launching the ordinary configured Uoink and filesystem connectors.
+
+The Python guard in `scripts/install_receipt/p4_common.py` was installed only into the bundled runtime (`app/python/python.exe`). It executes inside that specific Python process and provides no OS-level containment for Electron or external connector processes. Windows Job Object cleanup in `scripts/install_receipt/p4_session.py` confirms that child processes terminated when closed; it does not establish what network or filesystem operations occurred before termination.
+
+Desktop GUI acceptance credit is withheld. For package-08, native observation is restricted to the isolated Uoink dashboard (`uoink_dashboard.py`).
+
+---
+
+## Inspected Artifacts
+
+All inspections were restricted to static source files under the repository and the incident extract. No live databases, user profile configurations, authentication stores, or network endpoints were accessed.
