+
+## 1. Discard of CLAUDE_USER_DATA_DIR During Packaged Startup
+
+The integrator in `_scratch/native_gui07_driver.py` (lines 61–65) attempted to isolate Claude Desktop by writing a single-server config to a temporary folder and passing `CLAUDE_USER_DATA_DIR`:
+
+```python
+with (data / 'claude_desktop_config.json').open('x', encoding='utf8') as f:
+    json.dump({'mcpServers': config['mcpServers']}, f, indent=2)
+env['CLAUDE_USER_DATA_DIR'] = str(data)
+record['desktop_data_dir'] = str(data)
+gui = start([r'C:\Program Files\WindowsApps\Claude_1.49585.0.0_x64__pzs8sxrjxfjjc\app\claude.exe'], 'window', env)
+```
+
+The static source of `Claude_1.49585.0.0` at `_scratch/desktop-startup12-static/.vite/build/index.pre.js` shows why this failed. At character offset 891438:
+
+```javascript
+nW(!1),aW(!1);var QJ=rW();E.app.isPackaged&&!QJ&&(delete process.env.CLAUDE_USER_DATA_DIR,delete process.env.SSLKEYLOGFILE,delete process.env.sslkeylogfile),QU($J());
+```
+
+The function `rW()` (defined at offset 848479) verifies developer authorization:
+
+```javascript
+function rW(){
+  let e=process.env.CLAUDE_CDP_AUTH,t=process.env.CLAUDE_USER_DATA_DIR;
+  if(!e||!t)return!1;
+  let n=e=>(console.warn(`CDP auth rejected: ${e}`),!1),r=e.split(".");
+  if(r.length!==3)return n("malformed token (expected 3 dot-separated parts)");
+  let[i,a,o]=r,s=`${i}.${a}`;
+  if(Buffer.from(a,"base64").toString()!==t)return n("userData path mismatch");
+  let c=parseInt(i,10);
+  if(isNaN(c))return n("invalid timestamp");
+  let l=Date.now()-c;
+  if(l<0||l>eW)return n(`token expired (age: ${Math.round(l/1e3)}s)`);
+  try{
+    let e=re.createPublicKey($U);
+    return re.verify(null,Buffer.from(s),e,Buffer.from(o,"base64"))?!0:n("invalid signature")
+  }catch{
+    return n("signature verification threw")
+  }
+}
+```
+
+When `claude.exe` is run from the WindowsApps package, `E.app.isPackaged` evaluates to `true`. Without a valid token in `CLAUDE_CDP_AUTH` signed by the vendor's embedded public key `$U`, `QJ` evaluates to `false`. The application executes:
+
+```javascript
+delete process.env.CLAUDE_USER_DATA_DIR
+```
+
+Later in initialization (offset 892053), the code checks whether the variable exists:
+
+```javascript
+if(process.env.CLAUDE_USER_DATA_DIR){
+  let e=process.env.CLAUDE_USER_DATA_DIR;
+  E.app.setPath("userData",e),E.app.setPath("logs",h.default.resolve(e,"Logs"))
+}
+```
+
+Because the variable was deleted, `E.app.setPath("userData", e)` was skipped. The application fell back to its default paths under the user profile (`%APPDATA%\Claude` / `%LOCALAPPDATA%`). It loaded the user's real `claude_desktop_config.json`, which defined the ordinary system Uoink connector and filesystem connector, completely bypassing `run/user-data/claude_desktop_config.json`.
+
